  "receipt": "reports/v0-s3/product-gate0/implementation-native-custody-correction-01/native-custody-correction-01.receipt.json",
  "root_decisions": {
    "a_media_tools": "The ffmpeg, ffprobe and VIDEO_PROBE_BACKEND binding belongs to the N2 deployment and driver adapter. The closed plan of N1 is not widened and no media assembly completeness is claimed here.",
    "b_remaining_budget": "The real remaining balance of N3 comes from the original local_program_authority that verifies the original child and ledger and it is held by the parent. The parameter of N1 is a limit check only. The grant authority of this package stays NOT_VERIFIED and this package reads no ledger.",
    "c_nonce": "The nonce is produced by the parent and it enters through the fixed --nonce argument of the broker. It is not put into the plan and no arbitrary extra command line argument is added. The nonce binds the session and it never grants a custody over a pid.",
    "d_original_handle": "The parent holds the original creation handle of the broker and the job object of the round. No worker pid is adopted. The existing S2 wrapper.pid and _prove_listener_owned stay frozen and N2 needs an explicit compatibility adapter that consumes the original owner facts. No pid file is forged and no S2 proof is skipped.",
    "e_log_reference": "The log reference of the closed plan is judged with the Windows path semantics of the round and not with the semantics of the host that runs the check.  A drive absolute, a drive relative, a UNC, a backslash, a POSIX absolute, a traversal and an alternate data stream reference are refused in the production validate_launch_plan before any job, any process and any log exists.  The broker validates the plan again before it consumes it.",
    "f_facade_codes": "The in process facade fails with the stable broker code of the production source at the same position and it refuses an unknown failure point.  The facade proves the branches that it drives and it proves nothing about a real Windows API.",
    "g_erratum": "The reply body of the root validation plan 01 already carried the correct last character c of the coordinator digest.  The attribution of the previous report, that the root had copied the last character wrongly, does not match that original message and is corrected here.  The root did not notice that the test module still carried the wrong literal; that is a limitation of the static check and not a deliberate injection.  The old report and the old correction notes are kept byte for byte and the history is not rewritten.",
    "h_receipt_tail": "The trailing characters of the old runner receipt are a format property of the root receipt and not a product failure.  The original bytes are kept and the next root runner only writes the tail newline correctly.  No historical test result is changed and the old fifty four nodes are not rerun for it."
  },
  "scope": "One offline validation batch of the N1 parent owned native custody foundation after the N1 correction 01.  The batch is the selected subset of the plan: the eight failed nodes of the previous batch, the new path boundaries and the success, failure and cleanup nodes that are directly related to the changed fake facade.  It is not a rerun of the fifty four nodes and it is not a rerun of any earlier set.  No native execution, no service, no model, no GPU, no port, no media, no network, no download.",
